'''''Linaria maroccana''''' is a species of flowering plant in the [[Plantaginaceae|plantain family]] known by the common names '''annual toadflax''' and '''Moroccan toadflax'''.<ref name="PlantAtlas">{{cite web |title=Annual Toadflax ''Linaria maroccana'' Hook.f. |website=PlantAtlas |url=https://plantatlas2020.org/atlas/2cd4p9h.nm6 |access-date=2026-07-02}}</ref><ref name="Thorogood">{{cite book |last=Thorogood |first=Chris |title=Field guide to the wild flowers of the western Mediterranean |publisher=Kew publishing Royal Botanic Gardens |publication-place=Richmond |date=2016 |isbn=978-1-84246-616-2 |page=476}}</ref> It is [[endemism|endemic]] to [[Morocco]].<ref name="POWO">{{cite web |title=''Linaria maroccana'' Hook.f. |website=Plants of the World Online |date=2020-05-25 |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:804758-1 |access-date=2026-07-02}}</ref><ref>{{GRIN | accessdate = 19 January 2018}}</ref> 

It is an annual herb growing erect to a height of {{convert|40|cm|in|abbr=on|0}}, its stem with linear to elliptic leaves {{convert|2|–|4|cm|in|abbr=on|1}} long. The [[inflorescence]] is a [[raceme]] of flowers occupying the top of the stem. At the base of each flower is a [[sepal|calyx]] with five narrow, pointed lobes. The flower is {{convert|15|–|20|mm|in|abbr=on|1}} long with five lobes arranged into two lips with a straight spur at the back. The flower is violet-purple, with a small yellow or white spot near the throat.<ref name="Thorogood"/>

It is readily available as an [[ornamental plant]] for the [[flower garden]],<ref name = RHSPF/> though many cultivated plants are [[hybrid (biology)|hybrids]] with other closely related species.<ref name="Thorogood"/> As an [[introduced species]] it has become locally [[naturalisation (biology)|naturalised]], including in [[Great Britain]],<ref name="PlantAtlas"/> and [[California]].<ref>[http://ucjeps.berkeley.edu/cgi-bin/get_JM_treatment.pl?7177,7370,7374 Jepson Manual Treatment]</ref>  

The [[cultivar group]] Fairy Bouquet has gained the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]].<ref name = RHSPF>{{cite web | url= https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/310926/i-Linaria-maroccana-i-Fairy-Bouquet-Group/Details | title = RHS Plantfinder - ''Linaria maroccana'' Fairy Bouquet Group | website = www.rhs.org | accessdate=22 March 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url= https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/pdfs/agm-lists/agm-ornamentals.pdf | title = AGM Plants - Ornamental | date = July 2017 | page = 60 | publisher = Royal Horticultural Society | website = www.rhs.org | accessdate = 22 March 2018}}</ref> [[Dwarfing|Dwarf]] cultivars are also available.

